First Profile install attempt failed after a successful build because the
script passed `PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER=com.vectorblanco.hydracam.dev` as a
global xcodebuild override. That changed embedded plugin framework bundle IDs
too, and iOS rejected the install with duplicate framework identifiers:

`photo_manager.framework` and `disk_space_plus.framework` both appeared with
bundle identifier `com.vectorblanco.hydracam.dev`.

The fix was to set the Runner Profile build configuration bundle identifier in
`ios/Runner.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj` and remove the global
`PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER` xcodebuild argument from
`scripts/ios_icon_launch_dev.sh`. The later Profile build/install command
passed and installed bundle ID `com.vectorblanco.hydracam.dev`.
